#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/getting-started/concepts.md:70
msgid "Data formats you will meet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/getting-started/concepts.md:72
msgid ""
"**GeoTIFF / COG.** Raster data. A *Cloud-Optimized* GeoTIFF is internally "
"tiled so a client can fetch just part of it over HTTP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/getting-started/concepts.md:73
msgid "**SAFE.** The Sentinel product folder, usually delivered zipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/getting-started/concepts.md:74
msgid ""
"**SLC and GRD.** Sentinel-1 *Single Look Complex* (phase preserved; needed "
"for InSAR) and *Ground Range Detected* (amplitude only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/getting-started/concepts.md:75
msgid ""
"**STAC.** A standard JSON catalogue format for spatiotemporal assets, used "
"by many providers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/getting-started/concepts.md:76
msgid ""
"**GeoParquet and Zarr.** Cloud-native vector and array formats, available "
"through the `pygeofetch stream` conversion commands."
msgstr ""

